1. Repository Architecture (home-loan-orchestrator)A production-ready monorepo separates borrower intake, state assistance rules, lender submission (MISMO 3.4), and payment settlement into distinct modules:Plaintexthome-loan-orchestrator/
├── apps/
│   ├── borrower-portal/         # Frontend intake & status dashboard
│   └── webhook-gateway/         # Receives LOS status updates & payment events
├── packages/
│   ├── rules-engine/            # State DPA eligibility (e.g., Indiana IHCDA rules)
│   ├── mismo-mapper/            # Converts borrower JSON -> MISMO 3.4 XML / URLA (Form 1003)
│   ├── lender-connectors/       # API adapters for Encompass / wholesale portals
│   └── token-settlement/        # Smart contract vault + fiat off-ramp bridge (ACH/Wire)
├── schemas/
│   ├── borrower-profile.json
│   └── mismo-3.4.xsd
└── docker-compose.yml
2. Top 5 Mortgage Lenders & Integration RealityBased on U.S. origination volume, the top lenders operate via B2B wholesale broker portals or ICE Encompass APIs rather than public intake email addresses:LenderPrimary ChannelIntegration & Webhook MechanismPennymacWholesale / CorrespondentPOWER+ Portal / MISMO 3.4 upload & B2B APIRocket MortgageRetail & Rocket Pro TPORocket Pro TPO Partner API & milestone webhooksUnited Wholesale Mortgage (UWM)Wholesale BrokerBlink+ / UWM Partner API & webhook subscriptionsAmeriHome MortgageCorrespondentSeller Portal / MISMO 3.4 & Encompass Partner ConnectCrossCountry MortgageRetail / DistributedICE Encompass Developer Connect webhooksHow to wire the webhooks:Outbound (Application Submission): Generate a standardized Uniform Residential Loan Application (URLA / Fannie Mae Form 1003) serialized as MISMO 3.4 XML. Submit it via your LOS (such as ICE Encompass or Arive) or a lender's partner API.Inbound (Status Updates): Configure HTTPS POST webhook endpoints with HMAC signature verification (X-Webhook-Signature) to listen for loan milestone changes (ApplicationSubmitted, Underwriting, ClearToClose, Funded).Email Fallback (inbound-parse): For lenders or local housing agencies that only communicate via email, route a dedicated domain (e.g., loans@yourdomain.com) through SendGrid Inbound Parse or AWS SES to convert incoming status emails into JSON webhook payloads.3. State First-Time Homebuyer Programs (Indiana Example)Your rules-engine package can evaluate borrower eligibility against state Housing Finance Agency (HFA) guidelines before generating the application packet. In Indiana, the primary programs are administered by the Indiana Housing and Community Development Authority (IHCDA):IHCDA First Step Program: Combines a 30-year fixed-rate mortgage (FHA or Conventional) with down payment assistance (DPA) up to 5% of the purchase price (structured as a 0% interest, non-forgivable second lien due upon sale, refinance, or maturity).IHCDA Next Home Program: Provides up to 3.5% in down payment assistance; open to both first-time and repeat buyers who meet income and purchase price limits.IHCDA Step Down Program: A rate-only option for qualifying first-time homebuyers who do not require down payment assistance.FHLBank Indianapolis HomeBoost: Offers down payment assistance for households at or below 120% of Area Median Income (AMI) through participating member banks.Local Municipal Grants: City-level programs such as Evansville Down Payment Assistance (up to $15,000 for households under 80% AMI) and South Bend Community Homebuyers.
